
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# LOGOS prototype 3: early warning of failure paths (simulation)\n",
    "\n",
    "Question: can a window of recent signals warn of a coming failure earlier, and with fewer false alarms, than a simple threshold on the current value?\n",
    "\n",
    "**This is a simulation, not real driving data.** The simulator is written by us: a hidden stress level builds along a path to failure (bad weather, sensor drift), sometimes recovers, and sometimes a fault happens abruptly with no warning signs. The vehicle only sees noisy indirect signals (model disagreement, perception confidence, frame drops).\n",
    "Two versions are compared: without and with harmless short spikes (tunnels, sun glare). The result depends on those assumptions, so it shows when temporal context helps, not how well it works on real vehicles.\n",
    "\n",
    "Runtime: about 1 minute on a normal Colab CPU."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: simulator and evaluation tools"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import HistGradientBoostingClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "\n",
    "H = 30      # label: failure within next H seconds\n",
    "W = 20      # look-back window (seconds)\n",
    "L = 60      # an alarm counts as a real warning only if it fires within L seconds before a failure\n",
    "\n",
    "def simulate_episode(rng, T=900, glare=True, sudden_frac=0.25):\n",
    "    \"\"\"One vehicle, one drive. A hidden stress level rises along a 'path to failure'\n",
    "    (bad weather, sensor drift) and sometimes recovers before failing.\n",
    "    glare=True adds short harmless spikes in the signals (tunnels, sun glare).\n",
    "    sudden_frac = share of drives with an abrupt fault that has no warning signs.\"\"\"\n",
    "    base = max(0.05 + 0.03 * rng.standard_normal(), 0.0)\n",
    "    level = np.full(T, base)\n",
    "    n_events = rng.integers(0, 3)\n",
    "    starts = np.sort(rng.integers(50, T - 150, size=n_events))\n",
    "    for st in starts:\n",
    "        rise = rng.integers(40, 160)\n",
    "        peak = rng.uniform(0.4, 1.1)\n",
    "        hold = rng.integers(10, 80)\n",
    "        fall = rng.integers(30, 120)\n",
    "        shape = np.concatenate([np.linspace(0, peak, rise), np.full(hold, peak), np.linspace(peak, 0, fall)])\n",
    "        end = min(T, st + len(shape))\n",
    "        level[st:end] += shape[:end - st]\n",
    "    s = np.clip(level, 0, 1.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "    hazard = 0.12 / (1 + np.exp(-14 * (s - 0.85)))\n",
    "    sudden_t = rng.integers(100, T) if rng.random() < sudden_frac else None\n",
    "    fail_t = None\n",
    "    for t in range(T):\n",
    "        if (sudden_t is not None and t == sudden_t) or rng.random() < hazard[t]:\n",
    "            fail_t = t\n",
    "            break\n",
    "    end = T if fail_t is None else fail_t + 1\n",
    "\n",
    "    conf = 0.95 - 0.35 * s + 0.06 * rng.standard_normal(T)\n",
    "    disagree = 0.04 + 0.40 * s + 0.08 * rng.standard_normal(T)\n",
    "    drops = 0.02 + 0.25 * s + 0.06 * rng.standard_normal(T)\n",
    "    speed = 15 + 3 * rng.standard_normal(T)\n",
    "    if glare:\n",
    "        for _ in range(rng.integers(2, 6)):\n",
    "            g0 = rng.integers(0, T - 12)\n",
    "            gl = rng.integers(3, 10)\n",
    "            amp = rng.uniform(0.25, 0.5)\n",
    "            disagree[g0:g0 + gl] += amp\n",
    "            drops[g0:g0 + gl] += amp * 0.6\n",
    "            conf[g0:g0 + gl] -= amp * 0.5\n",
    "    X = np.stack([conf, disagree, drops, speed], axis=1)[:end]\n",
    "    return X, fail_t, end\n",
    "\n",
    "def window_features(X):\n",
    "    T, d = X.shape\n",
    "    feats, idx = [], []\n",
    "    tt = np.arange(W); tt_c = tt - tt.mean()\n",
    "    for t in range(W, T):\n",
    "        w = X[t - W:t]\n",
    "        mean = w.mean(0); last = w[-1]\n",
    "        slope = (tt_c[:, None] * (w - mean)).sum(0) / (tt_c ** 2).sum()\n",
    "        std = w.std(0)\n",
    "        feats.append(np.r_[mean, last, slope, std]); idx.append(t)\n",
    "    return np.array(feats), np.array(idx)\n",
    "\n",
    "def build_dataset(n_episodes, seed, **kw):\n",
    "    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n",
    "    F, y, ep_id, tpos, fail_times = [], [], [], [], {}\n",
    "    for e in range(n_episodes):\n",
    "        X, fail_t, end = simulate_episode(rng, **kw)\n",
    "        if end <= W + 1:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        f, idx = window_features(X)\n",
    "        label = np.zeros(len(idx), dtype=int)\n",
    "        if fail_t is not None:\n",
    "            label = (((fail_t - idx) <= H) & ((fail_t - idx) > 0)).astype(int)\n",
    "            fail_times[e] = fail_t\n",
    "        F.append(f); y.append(label); ep_id.append(np.full(len(idx), e)); tpos.append(idx)\n",
    "    return np.vstack(F), np.concatenate(y), np.concatenate(ep_id), np.concatenate(tpos), fail_times\n",
    "\n",
    "def prepare(ep_id, tpos, fail_times):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Precompute per-second helpers once (makes evaluation fast).\"\"\"\n",
    "    tf_row = np.full(len(ep_id), np.nan)\n",
    "    for e, tf in fail_times.items():\n",
    "        tf_row[ep_id == e] = tf\n",
    "    has_f = ~np.isnan(tf_row)\n",
    "    near = has_f & (tpos >= tf_row - L)                  # last L seconds before a failure\n",
    "    win = has_f & (tpos < tf_row) & (tpos >= tf_row - L)  # where an alarm counts as a real warning\n",
    "    return dict(ep=ep_id, t=tpos, tf=tf_row, healthy=~near, win=win,\n",
    "                n_fail=len(fail_times), hours=(~near).sum() / 3600.0)\n",
    "\n",
    "def evaluate_alarm(score, P, thr, gap=10):\n",
    "    alarm = score > thr\n",
    "    m = alarm & P[\"healthy\"]\n",
    "    ep, t = P[\"ep\"][m], P[\"t\"][m]\n",
    "    if len(t):\n",
    "        new = (np.diff(ep) != 0) | (np.diff(t) > gap)\n",
    "        events = 1 + int(new.sum())\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        events = 0\n",
    "    mw = alarm & P[\"win\"]\n",
    "    if mw.any():\n",
    "        e_w, t_w, tf_w = P[\"ep\"][mw], P[\"t\"][mw], P[\"tf\"][mw]\n",
    "        uniq = np.unique(e_w)\n",
    "        leads = []\n",
    "        for e in uniq:\n",
    "            k = e_w == e\n",
    "            leads.append(tf_w[k][0] - t_w[k].min())\n",
    "        warned = len(uniq)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        warned, leads = 0, []\n",
    "    return dict(fail_warned=warned / max(P[\"n_fail\"], 1),\n",
    "                median_lead=float(np.median(leads)) if leads else 0.0,\n",
    "                fa_per_hour=events / P[\"hours\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "def threshold_for_budget(score, P, target_per_hour):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Pick the alarm threshold (on TRAIN data) giving about `target_per_hour` false-alarm events/hour.\"\"\"\n",
    "    lo, hi = float(np.min(score)), float(np.max(score))\n",
    "    for _ in range(25):\n",
    "        mid = (lo + hi) / 2\n",
    "        if evaluate_alarm(score, P, mid)[\"fa_per_hour\"] > target_per_hour: lo = mid\n",
    "        else: hi = mid\n",
    "    return hi\n",
    "\n",
    "print('simulator ready')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: look at simulated drives"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Look at a few simulated drives: the hidden stress (dashed) and what the car can observe\n",
    "rng = np.random.default_rng(7)\n",
    "shown = 0\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(3, 1, figsize=(11, 8), sharex=False)\n",
    "while shown < 3:\n",
    "    X, fail_t, end = simulate_episode(rng, glare=True)\n",
    "    if fail_t is None or fail_t < 200:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    ax = axes[shown]\n",
    "    ax.plot(X[:, 1], label=\"model disagreement (guardian signal)\")\n",
    "    ax.plot(1 - X[:, 0], label=\"1 - perception confidence\", alpha=0.7)\n",
    "    ax.axvline(fail_t, color=\"k\", linestyle=\"--\", label=\"failure\")\n",
    "    ax.set_title(\"Drive %d: signals before a failure\" % (shown + 1))\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(\"seconds\"); ax.legend(loc=\"upper left\", fontsize=8)\n",
    "    shown += 1\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(\"logos_failpath_examples.png\", dpi=140)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: compare a simple threshold with window models\n",
    "\n",
    "The alarm threshold is chosen on training data to give a fixed number of false-alarm events per healthy hour, then scored on unseen test data.\n",
    "An alarm counts as a real warning only if it fires within 60 seconds before a failure."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def run(glare, n_tr=400, n_te=250):\n",
    "    Xtr, ytr, etr, ttr, ftr = build_dataset(n_tr, seed=1, glare=glare)\n",
    "    Xte, yte, ete, tte, fte = build_dataset(n_te, seed=2, glare=glare)\n",
    "    Ptr, Pte = prepare(etr, ttr, ftr), prepare(ete, tte, fte)\n",
    "    print(\"\\n=== harmless glare spikes in the data:\", glare, \"| test failures:\", len(fte), \"===\")\n",
    "    gb = HistGradientBoostingClassifier(max_iter=150, learning_rate=0.08, random_state=0).fit(Xtr, ytr)\n",
    "    sc = StandardScaler().fit(Xtr)\n",
    "    lr = LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000).fit(sc.transform(Xtr), ytr)\n",
    "    names = [\"threshold on current disagreement\", \"window model (boosting)\", \"window model (logistic)\"]\n",
    "    s_tr = [Xtr[:, 5], gb.predict_proba(Xtr)[:, 1], lr.predict_proba(sc.transform(Xtr))[:, 1]]\n",
    "    s_te = [Xte[:, 5], gb.predict_proba(Xte)[:, 1], lr.predict_proba(sc.transform(Xte))[:, 1]]\n",
    "    for target in (2, 6):\n",
    "        print(\"--- budget: about %d false-alarm events per healthy hour ---\" % target)\n",
    "        for name, a, b in zip(names, s_tr, s_te):\n",
    "            thr = threshold_for_budget(a, Ptr, target)       # chosen on TRAIN data only\n",
    "            r = evaluate_alarm(b, Pte, thr)                  # scored on unseen TEST data\n",
    "            print(\"%-34s warned %3.0f%% of failures | median lead %2.0fs | false alarms %.1f/hour\"\n",
    "                  % (name, 100 * r[\"fail_warned\"], r[\"median_lead\"], r[\"fa_per_hour\"]))\n",
    "\n",
    "run(glare=False)\n",
    "run(glare=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## How to read the result\n",
    "- Fixed false-alarm budget: compare the share of failures warned in advance and the lead time.\n",
    "- Abrupt faults (25% of drives in this simulation) cannot be predicted, so no method can reach 100%.\n",
    "- If the window models win mainly when glare spikes are present, the gain comes from telling short harmless spikes from sustained trends. That is a property of how the data was built.\n",
    "- Next step: repeat on real data with real failures or annotated perception errors."
   ]
  }
 ],
